# .NET Backend

- Target `net10.0`, keep nullable and implicit usings on.
- Controllers/Minimal APIs only orchestrate; call Application use cases.
- Register dependencies in composition root; no service locator.
- Use async APIs end-to-end with `CancellationToken`.
- Validation belongs at Application boundary (FluentValidation or equivalent), not buried in controllers.
- Prefer explicit DTOs for request/response contracts.
- Keep Domain free of EF Core, ASP.NET, and HTTP types.
- Infrastructure owns `DbContext`, migrations, and external integrations.
- Prefer Central Package Management (`Directory.Packages.props`) for multi-project solutions.
- Use `Directory.Build.props` for shared build settings across solution projects.
- Structured logging only; never log secrets or full PII.
- After meaningful backend changes, run `dotnet build` and relevant `dotnet test`.

## Documentation comments

When adding or modifying backend code, document **what** and **why** — not a line-by-line restatement of the code.

| Scope | Required | Format |
|-------|----------|--------|
| New file | Yes, when role is not obvious from the name | One-line file header comment or type-level `<summary>` on the primary type |
| Public class/record/interface | Yes | XML `<summary>` describing responsibility |
| Handler, service, store, controller action | Yes | XML `<summary>` on the type or action method |
| Private helper / obvious one-liner | No | Skip unless business rule is non-obvious |

Rules:

- Prefer XML doc comments (`///`) for types and public members; use `//` only for short file headers or non-public internals.
- Summarize **purpose, boundary, and side effects** (e.g. "Persists refresh-token rotation with optimistic concurrency").
- Do **not** comment every property, parameter, or trivial getter unless the name alone is insufficient.
- Do **not** duplicate OpenAPI metadata in prose comments when `[ProducesResponseType]` and DTO `<summary>` already cover the contract.
- Keep comments in English; match the language of existing files in the same folder.

```csharp
// Issues access/refresh tokens and coordinates refresh-token family rotation.
public sealed class AuthTokenIssuer(...) { }

/// <summary>Creates a user account when self-service registration is enabled.</summary>
public sealed class RegisterUser(...) { }

/// <summary>Rotates refresh tokens and issues a new access token.</summary>
[HttpPost("refresh")]
public async Task<IActionResult> Refresh(...) { }
```
